Commit 94b0ba41, parked on phase/8.4 (tag deleted 2026-10-16)
Subject: feat(pathogen-detection): narrow isolate_search by location and collection year

Card 28 (2026-09-25, DECISIONS.md): an isolate question can narrow by
location and collection year, not only by resistance gene.

Adds two optional, additive filters to the isolate_search branch:
location (a boundary-aware, case-folded prefix match against
geo_loc_name) and collection_year_min/collection_year_max (parsed off
the mixed-precision collection_date cell, never counting a missing or
unparseable date as a match). Both default to None so every existing
construction site keeps working unchanged.

core/isolate_search.py extracts a collection-year range from five
date phrases (since/before/between/through/in), a closed grammatical
class with no model call, the same discipline the existing gene-token
regex uses. Location is deliberately not extracted from free text:
mapping a person's words to the file's INSDC country spelling needs a
real resolver, not a hardcoded word list (DECISIONS.md 2026-09-24),
and the gap plus the exact change needed in core/graph.py are named
in the builder report.

Proof: 228 unit tests across the five touched files, ruff/isort
clean, and one live run against the real FTP file (E. coli, blaKPC,
USA, since 2020): 580 matches out of 584,992 rows scanned, 20 shown,
exact count, 21.26s.


