+## Card 28 (2026-09-25): narrowing by collection year, and the location gap
+
+Product-owner decision, 2026-09-25 (DECISIONS.md): "An isolate question can
+narrow by location and collection year, not only by resistance gene." Two
+different answers for the two filters, because one is a structural date
+phrase and the other is an open-ended name:
+
+Collection year IS parsed here, by `_find_collection_years`, the same way
+`_GENE_TOKEN` parses a gene spelling: a fixed rule over the question's own
+words, no model call, no vocabulary. "since 2020", "before 2015", "between
+2018 and 2020", "through 2021" and a bare "in 2021" are function-word
+patterns, a closed, finite class exactly like the grammar-word stopword list
+`core.graph`'s topic-search comment describes, not a growing pile of named
+entities. `plan_calls` threads the result into
+`PathogenDetectionInput`'s `collection_year_min`/`collection_year_max`.
+
+Location is NOT parsed here, on purpose. `pathogen_detection_schemas.py`'s
+own design decision 6 states why: a `geo_loc_name` cell is spelled in the
+INSDC controlled vocabulary ("USA", not "the United States"), and mapping a
+person's own words to that vocabulary needs a name lookup, either a live
+model classification or a verified reference table, not a hand-built list
+of country synonyms invented for this ticket (DECISIONS.md 2026-09-24, "no
+hardcoded decisions": the same trap `core.graph`'s own topic-search comment
+names, "the next question names a diet, a sport, an occupation or a
+country"). `IsolateQuestion.location` and `plan_calls`'s pass-through both
+exist so the plumbing is ready the moment a real resolver exists; nothing
+in this file guesses at filling it. THE EXACT CHANGE NEEDED ELSEWHERE: as of
+this ticket, `core/graph.py`'s `think_node` (around the call to
+`isolate_search.parse_isolate_question` near line 2233) has no location or
+country extraction of any kind for any tool, so there is no existing
+extractor to redirect here. Building one is a `core/graph.py` change, out
+of this ticket's file fence and out of scope per `v1-scope-boundary`'s
+spirit until a resolver design is chosen; it is not a two-line addition to
+this module.
+
